  "label": "Religious Coercion",
  "description": "The use of religious doctrine or authority to pressure or control individuals' behavior. The meme's intent to invoke a sense of accountability or fear of divine judgment can be interpreted as a form of religious coercion, which may be perceived as harmful when used to pressure or shame individuals, particularly in contexts where religious authority is leveraged to enforce social norms.",
